# Low Water, Act 2: the second dawn. The town meets about the gale; which lamps it can light.
# Director's file, 2026-10-17. Plan: design/ACT2-PLAN.md beat 17. Entered from ev2.dawn at 06:02.
# The choice sets Act 3's map of light (var light_* = 1 for each lamp kept for the gale).

# ---- new ids
@fact dawn2.met
@var gale_lamps
default: 0
@var light_mother
default: 0
@var light_steps
default: 0
@var light_porthole
default: 0
@var light_gut
default: 0
@var light_balance
default: 0
@var light_hill
default: 0
@var light_bulb
default: 0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the meeting
@node dawn2.start
place: weigh_in
cost: 4
do: set(dawn2.met)
nar: Sea smoke on the harbour, a white fur on black water, and the weigh-house full of people standing in their coats.
nar: The masters Dace and Orme stand together by the door with their hats on. Their barges are whole, and so is the Patience's paraffin. {when: var.spit_cargo == saved}
nar: The masters Dace and Orme stand apart. The Patience's paraffin is in the Board's shed, labelled SALVAGE FOR THE INSURER. {when: var.spit_cargo == taken}
nar: A strippers' boat lies at the bottom of the quay steps where the flood left it, deep with casks, and nobody in the room will say whose it is. {when: var.spit_cargo == adrift}
nar: Somebody near the door says the Shelf's name, low, to somebody else. They were on the Spit, and they know who saw them. {when: has(spit.named_back)}
nar: Two Lamplighters at the back are telling a third about a coat on the Spit that was not where it should have been. {when: has(book.spit_coat)}
nar: The Glass has been passed from hand to hand since half past five. It reads lower than anyone in the room has seen it read.
inst: THE GLASS: Nine hundred and seventy-one, and going down a step at a time like somebody leaving a house. Wind tonight, darling. From the south-west, and all of it.
line: KEEL: The Board has called the town. The Board has oil for three lamps through a gale, and men for three, and not one more.
line: KEEL: A ship takes the dog-leg on Mother, or on two lamps in a line: the steps post over the balance, or the hill lamps over the Gasholder. Or a light on the Spit itself, in the Old Light, if anybody could get one out there. Any other lamp by itself is only somewhere to steer at.
nar: The Alderman is not here. Mrs Pellow stands in her place at the back, holding her employer's gloves. {when: has(ink.crake)}
nar: The Alderman stands at the back in her grey, which reads the same in this light as in every other. {when: !has(ink.crake)}
voice: smallprint: The hill keeps a hand at its own panel, by standing order, within six minutes. Mother never had one. {when: has(hill.order_restrike), dc: 5}
nar: He drips on the weighbridge. Nobody moves away from him. In a room this full there is nowhere to move.
go: dawn2.room

@node dawn2.room
hub: yes
place: weigh_in
nar: Three lamps. The town looks at the Shelf, because the Shelf has a column for everything. {when: var.gale_lamps == 0}
nar: Chalked on the weigh-house board under LAMPS FOR THE GALE: {when: var.gale_lamps > 0}
nar: MOTHER. {when: var.light_mother == 1}
nar: THE STEPS POST. {when: var.light_steps == 1}
nar: THE BRINE'S PORTHOLE. {when: var.light_porthole == 1}
nar: THE GUT'S WIRES. {when: var.light_gut == 1}
nar: THE BALANCE. {when: var.light_balance == 1}
nar: THE HILL. {when: var.light_hill == 1}
nar: THE OLD BULB. {when: var.light_bulb == 1}
opt: "Mother." -> dawn2.mother ? var.light_mother == 0 & var.gale_lamps < 3 & var.lens != broken
opt: "Mother, though she is broken." -> dawn2.mother.broken ? var.light_mother == 0 & var.gale_lamps < 3 & var.lens == broken
opt: "The post at the top of the steps." -> dawn2.steps ? var.light_steps == 0 & var.gale_lamps < 3
opt: "The Brine's porthole lamp." -> dawn2.porthole ? var.light_porthole == 0 & var.gale_lamps < 3 & has(lamp.porthole.lit)
opt: "The Gut's wire lamps." -> dawn2.gut ? var.light_gut == 0 & var.gale_lamps < 3 & has(lamp.gut.lit)
opt: "The lamp on the balance." -> dawn2.balance ? var.light_balance == 0 & var.gale_lamps < 3
opt: "The white lamps on the hill." -> dawn2.hill ? var.light_hill == 0 & var.gale_lamps < 3 & !has(hill.dark)
opt: "The Old Bulb, back in the Gasholder." -> dawn2.bulb ? var.light_bulb == 0 & var.gale_lamps < 3 & (has(gasholder.procession_stopped) | var.mole2.bulb_end == vigil | var.mole2.bulb_end == knelt | var.mole2.bulb_end == measured | var.mole2.bulb_end == cold)
opt: "Rub the board clean and start again." -> dawn2.clear ? var.gale_lamps > 0
opt: "Let the town choose without the Shelf." -> dawn2.abstain ? var.gale_lamps == 0
opt: "That's three. Chalk it." -> dawn2.decided ? var.gale_lamps == 3
opt: "Fewer than three. Keep the oil." -> dawn2.decided ? var.gale_lamps > 0 & var.gale_lamps < 3

@node dawn2.clear
cost: 1
do: gale_lamps = 0; light_mother = 0; light_steps = 0; light_porthole = 0; light_gut = 0; light_balance = 0; light_hill = 0; light_bulb = 0
nar: Sabine wipes the board with her sleeve. She does not say what it costs.
go: ^hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- each lamp, and who speaks for it
@node dawn2.mother
cost: 2
do: light_mother = 1; gale_lamps += 1
line: WENNA: She'll want a hand at the panel all night. Mine, then. {when: !has(cause.keeper)}
line: WENNA: Somebody will have to sit with her. They'll not want it to be me. {when: has(cause.keeper)}
line: PENHALLOW: Bearing of the Spit, two-forty by Mother. Without her, no bearing. Log it. {when: has(met.penhallow)}
nar: Green, a third of her; honest, if the green rings went. The town would rather a green light than none. {when: var.lens == whole | var.lens == saved}
nar: With her green rings gone she will burn with gaps in her, white where she is whole and dark where she lied. {when: var.lens == green_broken}
nar: Her own feeder is back on its brass links. When the quay goes dark in the gale, she will not go with it. {when: has(weigh2.feeder)}
nar: She is still on the quay board. When the gale takes the quay, it takes her. {when: !has(weigh2.feeder)}
go: ^hub

@node dawn2.mother.broken
cost: 2
do: light_mother = 1; gale_lamps += 1
line: KEEL: The Board did not break her for her to be lit like that.
nar: The arc behind a shattered lens throws light in pieces, every way at once. It will be seen. It will not be read.
voice: precedent: A light that cannot be steered by is not a light under the Shelf's terms. It is weather. {dc: 6}
go: ^hub

@node dawn2.steps
cost: 1
do: light_steps = 1; gale_lamps += 1
line: FENNICK: The steps are ours. We will keep it. {when: !has(quay.relic.taken) & has(lamp.steps_post.lit)}
line: FENNICK: That post has been dark since the Trust came. Give us the Board's oil and a new wick, and we will keep it. {when: !has(quay.relic.taken) & !has(lamp.steps_post.lit)}
line: FENNICK: Light it, then. We have kept nothing else of ours tonight. {when: has(quay.relic.taken)}
go: ^hub

@node dawn2.porthole
cost: 1
do: light_porthole = 1; gale_lamps += 1
line: SABINE: Our yard. Our oil. The town's eyes on our bins all night. A shilling a gust, love, and I'll not charge you.
go: ^hub

@node dawn2.gut
cost: 1
do: light_gut = 1; gale_lamps += 1
line: MARROW: The Gut lit in a gale. The Captain never saw it. {when: var.gut_vote2 != spratt}
line: SPRATT: The steward will see to the wires. That's me, if you were wondering. {when: var.gut_vote2 == spratt}
go: ^hub

@node dawn2.balance
cost: 1
do: light_balance = 1; gale_lamps += 1
nar: The lamp on the town balance: a light nobody owns, on a thing that weighs everybody. Nobody speaks for it, so nobody speaks against it.
line: HOBB: I'll fill it. I'm not to. I'll fill it. {when: !has(lamp.balance.lit)}
go: ^hub

@node dawn2.hill
cost: 1
do: light_hill = 1; gale_lamps += 1
line: PELLOW: The Alderman would want the hill lit. She would want me to say so. I have said so.
nar: White lamps on the hill: the hill will see the harbour, and the harbour will see the hill seeing it.
go: ^hub

@node dawn2.bulb
cost: 2
do: light_bulb = 1; gale_lamps += 1
line: FENNICK: Low light, low water, high wind. It has waited twelve years to be asked.
voice: undertow: An old bulb in a gasholder, lit for a storm by the Shelf. Write that up the tube and see what comes back. {dc: 5}
go: ^hub

@node dawn2.abstain
cost: 3
do: gale_lamps = 3; light_mother = 1; light_hill = 1; light_steps = 1
nar: The assessor puts the chalk down. The town chooses without the Shelf, as towns do: Mother, because she is Mother; the hill, because the Alderman's housekeeper is standing nearest the board; the steps post, because the deacon is standing next to her.
go: dawn2.decided

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- decided
@node dawn2.decided
cost: 3
nar: The board is read out, and the room hears who goes dark.
line: SABINE: The steps lit and my yard dark, then. The bins can drown. {when: var.light_steps == 1 & var.light_porthole == 0}
line: FENNICK: The Brine's bins before the Congregation's steps. We will kneel in the dark, then. {when: var.light_porthole == 1 & var.light_steps == 0}
line: PELLOW: The Gut lit and the hill not. The Alderman will look down at fish all night. {when: var.light_gut == 1 & var.light_hill == 0}
line: KEEL: A lamp on the balance and the Board's own office dark. The Board notes it. {when: var.light_balance == 1 & var.light_mother == 0}
line: MARROW: The hill lit, and the Gut can find its own way home. {when: var.light_hill == 1 & var.light_gut == 0}
line: WENNA: An old bulb on a hill, and her not. {when: var.light_bulb == 1 & var.light_mother == 0}
line: KEEL: Mother takes the most oil of any of them. Whatever else is chalked will burn short. {when: var.light_mother == 1 & var.gale_lamps == 3}
nar: The chalk squeaks on the last word. Somebody opens the weigh-house doors, and the sea smoke comes in round everybody's ankles like a dog that wants to be in the meeting.
nar: Out on the mole, nobody is lighting anything yet. It is morning. The gale is eleven hours off, coming up the coast like a rumour.
go: dawn2.shelf

@node dawn2.shelf
place: tube
cost: 3
nar: At twenty past six the tube thumps.
nar: SHELF: GALE ANTICIPATED. ASSESSOR WILL ATTEND. CLAIM 4471/G REMAINS OPEN.
nar: SHELF: CLERK REPORTS ASSESSOR LISTENING AT WALLS. NOTED. {when: has(typist.heard)}
nar: SHELF: COMPLAINT RECEIVED FROM THE ALDERMAN. NOTED. {when: has(ink.crake)}
line: PIP: The e's worse. It's sticking on every one now. Somebody's been typing all night. {when: !has(typist.heard)}
line: PIP: The e's worse. You heard it too, didn't you. Through the wall. {when: has(typist.heard)}
nar: She looks at the canister and not at the assessor, and puts it back on its hook very carefully, as if it were somebody's.
go: dawn2.sleep

@node dawn2.sleep
place: room
cost: 10
nar: The coat goes by the stove again. It steams. It has been wet two nights now, and the tide mark at its hem has a second line above the first.
nar: SECOND WATER ENDS.
end: act2.end
